## Java 17: new features that are not preview

| Feature                                                     | Simple explanation                                                                  |
| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1. Sealed Classes (JEP 409)                                 | Restrict which classes can extend a class or implement an interface.                |
| 2. Enhanced Pseudo-Random Number Generators (JEP 356)       | Provide a common API for different random-number algorithms.                        |
| 3. Restore Always-Strict Floating-Point Semantics (JEP 306) | Make floating-point calculations consistently follow strict rules across platforms. |
| 4. Strongly Encapsulate JDK Internals (JEP 403)             | Restrict access to internal JDK APIs that applications shouldn't rely on.           |
| 5. Context-Specific Deserialization Filters (JEP 415)       | Allow applications to choose deserialization filters based on the context.          |

The first four are major Java 17 changes; the fifth is a library/security enhancement introduced in the same release.&#x20;

